.TH "GEOLOCATIONCOORDINATES.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
GeolocationCoordinates.toJSON \- GeolocationCoordinates: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]GeolocationCoordinates\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable
plain object representing the \f[CR]GeolocationCoordinates\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]GeolocationCoordinates\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]accuracy\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]latitude\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]longitude\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]altitude\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]altitudeAccuracy\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]heading\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]speed\f[R]
.PP
Each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example obtains a \f[CR]GeolocationCoordinates\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
navigator.geolocation.getCurrentPosition((position) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  \f[B]const\f[R] coords = position.coords;

  \f[B]const\f[R] json = coords.toJSON();
  console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
  console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
  console.log(json.latitude); \f[I]// Same value as coords.latitude\f[R]
});
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
Within the callback from the previous example, the same object can be
serialized using \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the
\f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(coords));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqaccuracy\(dq: 12.5,
  \(dqlatitude\(dq: 53.125,
  \(dqlongitude\(dq: 8.75,
  \(dqaltitude\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqaltitudeAccuracy\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqheading\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqspeed\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R]
}
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]JSON\f[R]
